- no dependency was installed ad hoc; authoritative CI provisions the reviewed pinned OLP dependency.

## Artifact / retention / rollback

Adds:
- `src/marketplace/runtime/inbound_tcp_socket_factory.py`;
- three public runtime exports;
- `docs/bounded-python-tcp-socket-factory.md`;
- focused deterministic/security/source-guard tests;
- M54 wheel-membership test;
- package artifact gate + synthetic missing-member regression.

M54 retains no request/response bytes, peer data, credentials, certificates, queue/cache/log payloads, or content-bearing state. Project transient retention remains `EPHEMERAL <=10s`.

Source-acceptance blast radius is repository/package surface only. Rollback is an ordinary source revert; no real socket/listener/port/service/credential/certificate/schema/user data/production state is created by acceptance.

## Governance hold

Provider-side `main` protection remains independently unverified/disabled; repository procedural governance therefore remains mandatory.

This HIGH PR requires exact-head self-hosted `Marketplace conformance / acceptance`, explicit maintainer/security self-review provenance, zero unresolved threads, and then either an eligible independent approval or a valid PR-specific Section 7 owner authorization for the exact accepted head before SHA-guarded merge. Automated CI and maintainer self-review are not independent human review. Generic continuation instructions are not treated as merge authorization.

## Summary

Resolve #106 by freezing the built-in durable-provider persisted-state compatibility contract before v1.

### Redis
- new scalar/vector reservation JSON writes `schemaVersion: 1`;
- exact pre-v1 unversioned records remain readable/settleable in-place with no bulk migration;
- targeted lifecycle operations reject any present schema version other than `1` before mutation;
- lazy cleanup preflights the complete selected reservation/tombstone batch before any release/retention/deletion so future state cannot cause partial cleanup mutation;
- real-Redis regression coverage proves new v1 records, legacy compatibility, targeted future-version fail-closed, and cleanup-batch no-partial-mutation behavior.

### Firestore / Cloudflare
The provider-wide EN/JA contract records the already-existing boundaries:
- Firestore reservation/budget documents use `schemaVersion: 1` and reject unsupported versions;
- Cloudflare DO SQLite uses explicit schema v3 migrations and rejects future versions at startup.

### Operator contract
Bilingual guidance defines forward upgrade, conditional/unsupported rollback boundaries, backup/restore expectations, and the fact that Redis `prefix`/`hashTag`, Firestore `collectionPrefix`, or a fresh Durable Object namespace/class select fresh accounting state and therefore constitute a quota/replay reset.

## Safety

- no accounting reset or bulk state rewrite;
- unknown/newer authoritative state never becomes empty quota state;
- no retry behavior change;
- Redis cleanup validates before writes because Lua runtime errors do not roll back prior writes;
- npm publication remains separately authorized.

Closes #106 after CI and merged-main verification.

